.DS_Store
__pycache__/
/.idea/

# build artifacts
canonical/*.sqlite
manifests/.checksum_cache.json

# Experiment run system (expkit). Full policy: docs/artifacts-git-policy.md
#
# artifacts/ is NOT ignored wholesale. Everything stays on disk; Git keeps only
# what is small, diffable and worth citing -- run.json, source_manifest.json,
# summaries, metrics.jsonl, per-experiment metrics/status/command/manifest JSON,
# verify results and the derived-artifact registry.
#
# Excluded below: bulk logs, per-question CSVs, vectors, indexes, the model
# cache, and raw API traffic. To publish one run's complete evidence, name it
# explicitly:  git add -f artifacts/runs/<run_id>/
artifacts/model_cache/
artifacts/derived/embeddings/
artifacts/derived/indexes/
artifacts/derived/corpora/
artifacts/test-runs/
artifacts/runs/*/summary.csv
artifacts/runs/*/source.patch
artifacts/runs/**/stdout.log
artifacts/runs/**/stderr.log
artifacts/runs/**/per_question.csv

# NOTE: artifacts/runs/*/source_bundle.zip is deliberately NOT ignored.
# It is binary and undiffable, which normally earns exclusion, but the manifest
# is useless without it: source_manifest.json can DETECT that code differs while
# being unable to PRODUCE the code that ran, because 18 of the 25 fingerprinted
# source files in this repo are untracked and therefore absent from source.patch.
# Committing the manifest and ignoring the bundle would ship exactly that half-
# record. The bundle is ~100 KB per run; that is a cheap price for a run that can
# actually be restored.

# Raw API requests and responses. Treated as potentially SENSITIVE: they hold
# full prompts (document text and image descriptions, whose dataset licence may
# restrict redistribution) and verbatim model output, alongside provider request
# ids and quota details. Secrets are redacted by expkit/apilog.py, but redaction
# is not a licence to publish. Review before adding any of it with -f.
artifacts/api/

# Phase 3 (E35/E36) caches. Both are regenerable and neither is evidence:
# the action table rebuilds from canonical/ + retrieval/ in ~20 s, the per-cell
# checkpoints rebuild in ~40 min, and the authoritative record of every number
# is the run's metrics.json. Measured 2026-08-30: router/cache = 9.8 MB
# (two ~5 MB action tables plus 16 small cell JSONs). If it ever stops being
# small, that is the signal to bound it -- see docs/HANDOFF.md 5.4-19.
router/cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local research working set. Everything below stays on disk; none of it is
# evidence, and all of it is either downloadable or regenerable from what IS
# committed. Sizes measured 2026-08-31.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Model weights, 9.6 GB. Re-fetchable, and fetch.json pins the exact revision
# plus a per-file SHA-256, so identity survives without the bytes:
#   python -m retrieval.fetch_model BAAI/bge-large-en-v1.5 --check
models/
!models/*/fetch.json

# Corpora, indexes and vectors, ~1.2 GB. Rebuilt by retrieval/corpus.py,
# quote_corpus.py, dense.py and dense_chunks.py from canonical/ + the dataset.
retrieval/embeddings/
retrieval/e2e/
retrieval/*.sqlite
retrieval/*.pkl

# Phase 1A.5 outcome database and feature cache, 48 MB. Rebuilt by
# router/build_outcomes.py and router/features.py.
router/outcomes.sqlite
router/*.npz

# This session's scratch logs. Never evidence -- the authoritative record of
# every number is the run's metrics.json under artifacts/runs/.
tmp/
artifacts/logs/
